---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="How TwineLine works" description="Understand how TwineLine turns your photos into beautiful daily slideshows on your TV.">
  <div class="content-pane mx-auto max-w-4xl mt-6 sm:mt-10 mb-12 sm:mb-20 px-6 sm:px-10 py-8 sm:py-12">

    <!-- Intro -->
    <section class="pb-6 sm:pb-8">
      <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight leading-tight" style="color: var(--text-primary);">
        How TwineLine works
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--text-secondary);">
        TwineLine connects your photo libraries to a server that builds a fresh slideshow every day,
        then streams it to any screen in your house. Here are the most common ways to set it up.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Setup A: Smart TV + your computer -->
    <section class="py-6 sm:py-8" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--glass-border);">
      <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold mb-1" style="color: var(--accent);">Smart TV + your computer</h2>
      <p class="text-sm mb-5" style="color: var(--text-muted);">Best if your TV has Google TV or Fire TV built in. No extra hardware needed.</p>

      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center sm:items-stretch gap-2 sm:gap-0">
        <div class="glass p-3 sm:p-4 text-center flex-1 w-full sm:w-auto min-w-0 flex flex-col items-center justify-center">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 mb-1" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="color: var(--accent);">
            <path d="M6.5 19h11a4.5 4.5 0 0 0 1.09-8.87 6 6 0 0 0-11.18 0A4.5 4.5 0 0 0 6.5 19z" />
          </svg>
          <h4 class="text-xs font-semibold" style="color: var(--text-primary);">Your photos</h4>
        </div>

        <div class="flex items-center justify-center px-2 sm:px-3 py-1 sm:py-0" style="color: var(--accent);">
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 hidden sm:block" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 5l7 7-7 7" /></svg>
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 sm:hidden" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 13l7 7 7-7" /></svg>
        </div>

        <div class="glass p-3 sm:p-4 text-center flex-1 w-full sm:w-auto min-w-0 flex flex-col items-center justify-center" style="border-color: var(--accent); border-width: 1px;">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 mb-1" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="color: var(--accent);">
            <rect x="2" y="3" width="20" height="14" rx="2" /><path d="M8 21h8M12 17v4" />
          </svg>
          <h4 class="text-xs font-semibold" style="color: var(--text-primary);">Your computer</h4>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-col items-center justify-center px-2 sm:px-3 py-1 sm:py-0">
          <span class="text-[9px] font-medium uppercase tracking-wider mb-0.5" style="color: var(--text-muted);">WiFi</span>
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 hidden sm:block" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="color: var(--accent);"><path d="M5 12h14M13 5l7 7-7 7" /></svg>
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 sm:hidden" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="color: var(--accent);"><path d="M12 5v14M5 13l7 7 7-7" /></svg>
        </div>

        <div class="glass p-3 sm:p-4 text-center flex-1 w-full sm:w-auto min-w-0 flex flex-col items-center justify-center">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 mb-1" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="color: var(--accent);">
            <rect x="2" y="3" width="20" height="14" rx="2" /><path d="M8 21h8M12 17v4" />
          </svg>
          <h4 class="text-xs font-semibold" style="color: var(--text-primary);">Smart TV</h4>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="text-xs mt-3" style="color: var(--text-muted);">Cost: free. Runs when your computer is on.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Setup B: Streaming stick + your computer -->
    <section class="py-6 sm:py-8" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--glass-border);">
      <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold mb-1" style="color: var(--accent);">Streaming stick + your computer</h2>
      <p class="text-sm mb-5" style="color: var(--text-muted);">Best for older TVs without a built-in smart platform.</p>

      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center sm:items-stretch gap-2 sm:gap-0">
        <div class="glass p-3 sm:p-4 text-center flex-1 w-full sm:w-auto min-w-0 flex flex-col items-center justify-center">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 mb-1" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="color: var(--accent);">
            <path d="M6.5 19h11a4.5 4.5 0 0 0 1.09-8.87 6 6 0 0 0-11.18 0A4.5 4.5 0 0 0 6.5 19z" />
          </svg>
          <h4 class="text-xs font-semibold" style="color: var(--text-primary);">Your photos</h4>
        </div>

        <div class="flex items-center justify-center px-2 sm:px-3 py-1 sm:py-0" style="color: var(--accent);">
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 hidden sm:block" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 5l7 7-7 7" /></svg>
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 sm:hidden" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 13l7 7 7-7" /></svg>
        </div>

        <div class="glass p-3 sm:p-4 text-center flex-1 w-full sm:w-auto min-w-0 flex flex-col items-center justify-center" style="border-color: var(--accent); border-width: 1px;">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 mb-1" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="color: var(--accent);">
            <rect x="2" y="3" width="20" height="14" rx="2" /><path d="M8 21h8M12 17v4" />
          </svg>
          <h4 class="text-xs font-semibold" style="color: var(--text-primary);">Your computer</h4>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-col items-center justify-center px-2 sm:px-3 py-1 sm:py-0">
          <span class="text-[9px] font-medium uppercase tracking-wider mb-0.5" style="color: var(--text-muted);">WiFi</span>
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 hidden sm:block" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="color: var(--accent);"><path d="M5 12h14M13 5l7 7-7 7" /></svg>
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 sm:hidden" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="color: var(--accent);"><path d="M12 5v14M5 13l7 7 7-7" /></svg>
        </div>

        <div class="glass p-3 sm:p-4 text-center flex-1 w-full sm:w-auto min-w-0 flex flex-col items-center justify-center">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 mb-1" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="color: var(--accent);">
            <rect x="4" y="6" width="16" height="12" rx="1" /><path d="M2 18h20" />
          </svg>
          <h4 class="text-xs font-semibold" style="color: var(--text-primary);">Stick + TV</h4>
          <p class="text-[10px]" style="color: var(--text-muted);">HDMI</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="text-xs mt-3" style="color: var(--text-muted);">Cost: ~$30 one-time for the stick. Runs when your computer is on.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Setup C: All-in-one computer -->
    <section class="py-6 sm:py-8" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--glass-border);">
      <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold mb-1" style="color: var(--accent);">All-in-one computer</h2>
      <p class="text-sm mb-5" style="color: var(--text-muted);">Best for a dedicated mini PC that stays connected to the TV.</p>

      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center sm:items-stretch gap-2 sm:gap-0">
        <div class="glass p-3 sm:p-4 text-center flex-1 w-full sm:w-auto min-w-0 flex flex-col items-center justify-center">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 mb-1" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="color: var(--accent);">
            <path d="M6.5 19h11a4.5 4.5 0 0 0 1.09-8.87 6 6 0 0 0-11.18 0A4.5 4.5 0 0 0 6.5 19z" />
          </svg>
          <h4 class="text-xs font-semibold" style="color: var(--text-primary);">Your photos</h4>
        </div>

        <div class="flex items-center justify-center px-2 sm:px-3 py-1 sm:py-0" style="color: var(--accent);">
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 hidden sm:block" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 5l7 7-7 7" /></svg>
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 sm:hidden" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 13l7 7 7-7" /></svg>
        </div>

        <div class="glass p-3 sm:p-4 text-center flex-1 w-full sm:w-auto min-w-0 flex flex-col items-center justify-center" style="border-color: var(--accent); border-width: 1px;">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 mb-1" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="color: var(--accent);">
            <rect x="2" y="3" width="20" height="14" rx="2" /><path d="M8 21h8M12 17v4" />
          </svg>
          <h4 class="text-xs font-semibold" style="color: var(--text-primary);">Computer</h4>
          <p class="text-[10px]" style="color: var(--text-muted);">server + display</p>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-col items-center justify-center px-2 sm:px-3 py-1 sm:py-0">
          <span class="text-[9px] font-medium uppercase tracking-wider mb-0.5" style="color: var(--text-muted);">HDMI</span>
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 hidden sm:block" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="color: var(--accent);"><path d="M5 12h14M13 5l7 7-7 7" /></svg>
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 sm:hidden" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="color: var(--accent);"><path d="M12 5v14M5 13l7 7 7-7" /></svg>
        </div>

        <div class="glass p-3 sm:p-4 text-center flex-1 w-full sm:w-auto min-w-0 flex flex-col items-center justify-center">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 mb-1" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="color: var(--accent);">
            <rect x="2" y="3" width="20" height="14" rx="2" /><path d="M8 21h8M12 17v4" />
          </svg>
          <h4 class="text-xs font-semibold" style="color: var(--text-primary);">Your TV</h4>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="text-xs mt-3" style="color: var(--text-muted);">Cost: free (if you have a spare computer) or ~$150 for a mini PC.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Setup D: Cloud server -->
    <section class="py-6 sm:py-8" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--glass-border);">
      <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold mb-1" style="color: var(--accent);">Cloud server</h2>
      <p class="text-sm mb-5" style="color: var(--text-muted);">Best for always-on operation and access from anywhere.</p>

      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center sm:items-stretch gap-2 sm:gap-0">
        <div class="glass p-3 sm:p-4 text-center flex-1 w-full sm:w-auto min-w-0 flex flex-col items-center justify-center">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 mb-1" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="color: var(--accent);">
            <path d="M6.5 19h11a4.5 4.5 0 0 0 1.09-8.87 6 6 0 0 0-11.18 0A4.5 4.5 0 0 0 6.5 19z" />
          </svg>
          <h4 class="text-xs font-semibold" style="color: var(--text-primary);">Your photos</h4>
        </div>

        <div class="flex items-center justify-center px-2 sm:px-3 py-1 sm:py-0" style="color: var(--accent);">
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 hidden sm:block" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 5l7 7-7 7" /></svg>
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 sm:hidden" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 13l7 7 7-7" /></svg>
        </div>

        <div class="glass p-3 sm:p-4 text-center flex-1 w-full sm:w-auto min-w-0 flex flex-col items-center justify-center" style="border-color: var(--accent); border-width: 1px;">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 mb-1" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="color: var(--accent);">
            <path d="M6.5 19h11a4.5 4.5 0 0 0 1.09-8.87 6 6 0 0 0-11.18 0A4.5 4.5 0 0 0 6.5 19z" />
          </svg>
          <h4 class="text-xs font-semibold" style="color: var(--text-primary);">Hetzner cloud</h4>
          <p class="text-[10px]" style="color: var(--text-muted);">~$5/mo</p>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-col items-center justify-center px-2 sm:px-3 py-1 sm:py-0">
          <span class="text-[9px] font-medium uppercase tracking-wider mb-0.5" style="color: var(--text-muted);">Web</span>
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 hidden sm:block" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="color: var(--accent);"><path d="M5 12h14M13 5l7 7-7 7" /></svg>
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 sm:hidden" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="color: var(--accent);"><path d="M12 5v14M5 13l7 7 7-7" /></svg>
        </div>

        <div class="glass p-3 sm:p-4 text-center flex-1 w-full sm:w-auto min-w-0 flex flex-col items-center justify-center">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 mb-1" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="color: var(--accent);">
            <rect x="2" y="3" width="20" height="14" rx="2" /><path d="M8 21h8M12 17v4" />
          </svg>
          <h4 class="text-xs font-semibold" style="color: var(--text-primary);">Any screen</h4>
          <p class="text-[10px]" style="color: var(--text-muted);">TV, phone, tablet</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="text-xs mt-3" style="color: var(--text-muted);">Cost: ~$5/month (at least one month free with our referral link).</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Which setup is right for me -->
    <section class="py-6 sm:py-8" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--glass-border);">
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold mb-2" style="color: var(--text-primary);">Which setup is right for me?</h2>
      <p class="text-base mb-6" style="color: var(--text-secondary);">
        There is no wrong choice &mdash; you can change your setup anytime without losing your photos, face recognition data, or slideshows.
      </p>

      <!-- Comparison table -->
      <div class="glass p-5 sm:p-6 overflow-x-auto mb-6">
        <table class="w-full text-sm" style="color: var(--text-secondary);">
          <thead>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--glass-border);">
              <th class="text-left py-3 pr-4" style="color: var(--text-primary);"></th>
              <th class="text-left py-3 px-4" style="color: var(--text-primary);">Your computer</th>
              <th class="text-left py-3 pl-4" style="color: var(--text-primary);">Cloud (Hetzner)</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--glass-border);">
              <td class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium" style="color: var(--text-primary);">Cost</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4">Free forever</td>
              <td class="py-3 pl-4">~$5/month (at least 1 month free)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--glass-border);">
              <td class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium" style="color: var(--text-primary);">Always running?</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4">Only when your computer is on</td>
              <td class="py-3 pl-4">Yes, 24/7</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--glass-border);">
              <td class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium" style="color: var(--text-primary);">Access outside your home?</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4">No (home network only)</td>
              <td class="py-3 pl-4">Yes, from anywhere</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--glass-border);">
              <td class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium" style="color: var(--text-primary);">Fast AI analysis</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4">Standard speed</td>
              <td class="py-3 pl-4">Optional turbo mode ($10&ndash;$20 one-time)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium" style="color: var(--text-primary);">Best for</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4">Trying it out, single household</td>
              <td class="py-3 pl-4">Daily automated slideshows, families across multiple homes</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <!-- Recommendation -->
      <div class="glass p-5 sm:p-6" style="border-color: var(--accent); border-width: 1px;">
        <p class="font-semibold mb-2" style="color: var(--accent);">Our suggestion</p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--text-secondary);">
          Start with a <strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Hetzner cloud server</strong>. With our referral link, you get
          at least one month of free hosting. You get 24/7 operation, web access from your phone,
          and the option to run fast AI analysis on your whole photo library. If you decide to switch to your own
          computer later, you can migrate everything with a single command and run TwineLine for free going forward.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Quick decision guide -->
    <section class="py-6 sm:py-8" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--glass-border);">
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold mb-5" style="color: var(--text-primary);">Quick guide</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div class="flex gap-3 items-start">
          <div class="w-5 h-5 rounded-full flex-shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center mt-0.5" style="background: var(--accent);">
            <svg class="w-3 h-3" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" /></svg>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm" style="color: var(--text-secondary);">
            <strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">If your TV has Google TV or Fire TV built in</strong> &mdash; you only need to set up the server. No extra hardware.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-3 items-start">
          <div class="w-5 h-5 rounded-full flex-shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center mt-0.5" style="background: var(--accent);">
            <svg class="w-3 h-3" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" /></svg>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm" style="color: var(--text-secondary);">
            <strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">If your TV is an older model</strong> &mdash; add a streaming stick (~$30) that plugs into your TV.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-3 items-start">
          <div class="w-5 h-5 rounded-full flex-shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center mt-0.5" style="background: var(--accent);">
            <svg class="w-3 h-3" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" /></svg>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm" style="color: var(--text-secondary);">
            <strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">If you want to dedicate a computer to TwineLine</strong> &mdash; connect it directly to your TV with an HDMI cable. It handles everything.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-3 items-start">
          <div class="w-5 h-5 rounded-full flex-shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center mt-0.5" style="background: var(--accent);">
            <svg class="w-3 h-3" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" /></svg>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm" style="color: var(--text-secondary);">
            <strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Want it always on without managing a computer?</strong> &mdash; use a cloud server. Free for the first couple of months with our referral link.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Technical details (expandable) -->
    <section class="py-6 sm:py-8" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--glass-border);">
      <details class="glass p-5 sm:p-6">
        <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer" style="color: var(--text-primary);">How it works technically</summary>
        <div class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm" style="color: var(--text-secondary);">
          <p><strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Server:</strong> Python FastAPI application serving a REST API on port 8080.</p>
          <p><strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Player:</strong> Vue.js 3 single-page app optimized for streaming devices, rendered via the TwineLine app or any Chromium-based browser.</p>
          <p><strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Communication:</strong> WebSocket connection with a 1-second heartbeat. The server is the single source of truth for slideshow state &mdash; slide index, play/pause, timing. Clients are passive viewers.</p>
          <p><strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Database:</strong> SQLite (single-file, no setup required).</p>
          <p><strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Photo sources:</strong> Microsoft OneDrive (via Microsoft Graph API), local filesystem, Pixabay stock photos.</p>
          <p><strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Image processing:</strong> Pillow for optimization, OpenCV for face detection, FFmpeg for video transcoding.</p>
          <p><strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Face recognition:</strong> FaceNet model running locally on CPU (~2 GB model download, no cloud dependency, no GPU required).</p>
          <p><strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Multi-device sync:</strong> A lightweight signaling layer keeps all screens in sync. Only control messages travel through this layer &mdash; your photos never leave your network.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
